<title>USA: Sysco to merge two San Francisco units.</title>
<headline>Sysco to merge two San Francisco units.</headline>
<dateline>HOUSTON 1997-07-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Sysco Corp said Friday it would merge its two San Francisco area subsidiaries, Allied-Sysco Food Services Inc in Fremont and Sysco Avard Food Services Inc in Union City into one company.</p>
<p>The food distributor said it will not cut the subsidiaries' 1,200 employees, who represent about four percent of Sysco's total workforce.</p>
<p>The company said Sysco Avard will be able to offer 4,000 additional products, benefitting from Allied-Sysco's Fremont warehouse capacity.</p>
</text>
